Subject: [PATCH 0/5] Implement D3DKMT{Get,Set}ProcessSchedulingPriorityClass

OBS Studio 33 calls D3DKMTSetProcessSchedulingPriorityClass() from gdi32
when initializing its Direct3D 11 renderer, and currently crashes on the
unimplemented win32u stub.

The priority class is stored per process in the server, so that it can
be queried and changed through handles to other processes, with the
PROCESS_SET_INFORMATION / PROCESS_QUERY_LIMITED_INFORMATION access
checks. Setting the realtime class requires SeIncreaseBasePriorityPrivilege
to be enabled, otherwise STATUS_PRIVILEGE_NOT_HELD is returned, which OBS
only logs. The value doesn't affect GPU scheduling yet.

chatgptyukkuri (5):
  include: Add D3DKMT{Get,Set}ProcessSchedulingPriorityClass
    declarations.
  server: Store the GPU scheduling priority class of processes.
  win32u: Implement NtGdiDdDDI{Get,Set}ProcessSchedulingPriorityClass.
  gdi32: Export D3DKMT{Get,Set}ProcessSchedulingPriorityClass.
  win32u/tests: Add D3DKMT{Get,Set}ProcessSchedulingPriorityClass tests.

